We examine the decay width ratios $\Gamma(B 	o D\ell ar{
u})/\Gamma(B 	o D^*\ell ar{
u})$ and $\Gamma(B_c 	o D \ell  ar{
u})/\Gamma(B_c 	o D^*\ell  ar{
u})$ within the framework of the heavy quark expansion. Our analysis reveals that these ratios exhibit significant deviations from their respective heavy quark limit predictions of 1 and 1/3, with corrections of order $O(1/m_Q)$ reaching approximately 10%. These findings are consistent with recent experimental measurements.
